+## Proposed implementation waves
+
+Ordered by dependency + impact. Effort is rough (S = hours, M = a day-ish, L = multi-day). Filed beads are marked.
+
+### Wave 1 — Scoring-correctness criticals (engine bugs that produce wrong results) · effort L
+These are the three confirmed criticals plus the High-severity cricket extras bug — all in untested live-scorer component logic, all produce a wrong, user-visible, unrecoverable result.
+- **P0-1** (filed: scoreeasy-m39) — cricket test 3rd-innings premature end. *S–M*
+- **P0-3** (filed: scoreeasy-sjo) — single-set win-by-2 + fix the bug-locking test. *S*
+- **P0-4** (filed: scoreeasy-ayc) — tennis tournament `score1/score2` contract (fold in P1-9 tiebreak 7-6). *M*
+- **P0-5** (filed: scoreeasy-awy) — cricket no-ball/wide runs-off-the-delivery. *M*
+- Pull-in candidates (same engines, cheap to co-fix): **P1-8** (test follow-on label), **P1-9** (tiebreak 7-6, co-fixed with P0-4), **P1-10** (tennis phantom set).
+
+Rationale: highest correctness impact; do first because downstream waves (tournament integrity, stats) consume the values these engines emit.
+
+### Wave 2 — Tournament integrity · effort M–L
+Bracket/standings correctness once the scoring engines are trustworthy.
